{
  "name": "idle",
  "note": "(anim-rework S2, real-world standard, keyed by hand) The standing holstered idle, a relaxed trained-operator stance: upright (M6), feet about hip width (legs add 0.5 deg: about 9 cm a foot), knees soft and over the toes; alive but never fast over a 12 s cycle (KEYED_IDLE_PERIOD, one key a second): three slow breaths (the chest lifts 1.2 deg), the weight easing onto the right foot and back and onto the left (pelvis 1.2 cm, its loaded side up 1.2 deg), one slow head scan each way (18 deg right at 4-5 s, 15 deg left at 9-10 s, the chest turning a little with it); the arms hang relaxed along the sides (abd 4, elbows 12). Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from rest (the height adds to the legs' own reach drop). Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in toward the midline). Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
